course: dictionary
lesson: 6956
title: Paleness and what it tells us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Paleness means the state of being pale: having a light colour, or less colour than usual.
explain: «A hypo is blood sugar too low, from too much insulin, too little food or extra exercise; signs are shaking, sweating, paleness, crossness or confusion.» Here paleness is a sign in a body. The skin looks lighter than usual because the person is unwell.
explain: Look at the other signs in the list: shaking, sweating, crossness and confusion. They all show that something is wrong with the body, so paleness is a clue too. It is not about a painting or a colour chart.
fact: Paleness is a noun. You can talk about the paleness of a face or the paleness of a sky.
fact: «Paleness» means the state of being pale, with a light colour or less colour than usual.
fact: Paleness can also mean the lightness of a person's face when they are ill, tired or frightened.
fact: In health, paleness of the skin can be a sign of being unwell, cold or low on iron.
fact: In stories, a character's paleness often shows fear, shock or illness.
exercise: «A hypo is blood sugar too low, from too much insulin, too little food or extra exercise; signs are shaking, sweating, paleness, crossness or confusion.» In this sentence, what is paleness a sign of? | Eating too many sweets | Winning a race | *Being unwell, with lighter skin than usual | A bright, sunny day at the beach
exercise: Mum paints the sky in soft blue and white. Her art teacher says the paleness of the sky looks lovely. What does paleness mean here? | A loud, bright red | A cold, wet puddle | A dark, heavy shadow | *A light, soft colour
exercise: Find and copy one word from «A hypo is blood sugar too low, from too much insulin, too little food or extra exercise; signs are shaking, sweating, paleness, crossness or confusion.» that means being cross. | insulin | shaking | *crossness | sweating
test: In a story, a girl's paleness shows what? | A sunny holiday | A big plate of pasta | *Fear or shock | A new bike
test: Which word is closest in meaning to paleness, meaning lightness of a person's face? | Sharpness | Loudness | Darkness | *Lightness
exam: In health, what can paleness of the skin be a sign of? | Sunburn from a long day outside | *Being unwell, cold or low on iron | Winning a prize | Eating a big dinner
